# =====================================================================
#  .gitignore — Wazuh SOC Lab
#  Keeps secrets, credentials, and attack artifacts OUT of the repo.
#  (This file only takes effect when you use Git on the command line.
#   If you upload via the GitHub website, just don't select these files.)
# =====================================================================

# --- Secrets & credentials — NEVER commit these ---
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*credential*
api_key*.txt
secrets/

# Commit the sanitized example instead of the real agent/manager config
**/ossec.conf
!**/ossec.conf.example

# --- Attack artifacts ---
passwords.txt
wordlists/

# --- Logs & alert data ---
*.log
alerts.json
alerts.log

# --- Large / binary lab captures (don't belong in git) ---
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.evtx
*.ova
*.vmdk
*.vmx

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
